!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/valid/a-tag-at-a-choice-naming-a-member-of-an-abstract-variant-selects-it-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.4, [TSON-SCHEMA] §7.2"
  description: """
    A tag at a choice names a variant, or a type that IS-A exactly one variant. At `item`, `( text | shape )` with
    `shape` abstract, `!circle` IS-A `shape` alone, so it selects `shape` and the value is read there as at a
    position typed by `shape`: it validates as a `circle`, whose `r` the variant does not declare. A reader that
    takes the tag for a variant's name only finds no variant `circle`.
    """
  valid: _
}
